     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Here is the link to Pandoc:<div><a href=\"https://github.com/jgm/pandoc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/jgm/pandoc&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792497733088000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3smIDHB3SliahEs590B78e\">https://github.com/jgm/pandoc</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>I suspect however, that as of RStudio 0.98 you won&#39;t be needing it. Try this guide:</div><div><a href=\"https://support.rstudio.com/hc/en-us/articles/200486468-Authoring-R-Presentations\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://support.rstudio.com/hc/en-us/articles/200486468-Authoring-R-Presentations&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792497733088000&amp;usg=AOvVaw30rlGI3F61qWssK_DIhRIS\">https://support.rstudio.com/hc/en-us/articles/200486468-Authoring-R-Presentations</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>Also- </div><div>I would not have my hopes too high on ppt.Then again, there are several pdf readers that are aimed at presentations and not documents. Here is a nice list:</div><div><a href=\"http://superuser.com/questions/339404/solutions-for-presenting-pdf-slides-with-presenter-notes-on-second-display\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://superuser.com/questions/339404/solutions-for-presenting-pdf-slides-with-presenter-notes-on-second-display&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792497733088000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1o06dlNjIO9YehNnEA3V59\">http://superuser.com/questions/339404/solutions-for-presenting-pdf-slides-with-presenter-notes-on-second-display</a><br></div><div>I can give recommendations for linux. I have no idea which is a good alternative for Windows.<br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
